## File map
extract_pose.py   — Phase 1: single video → keyframes JSON + pose overlay video
process_dance.py  — Phase 2: batch runner over all clips in a dance folder
average_dance.py  — Phase 3: circular mean across clips → canonical motion file
pipeline_config.yaml — all tunable constants, no hardcoding allowed

## Folder structure enforced by the pipeline:
dances/
  {dance_name}/
    raw/               # user drops .mp4 files here
    processed/
      {clip_name}/
        {clip_name}_original.mp4
        {clip_name}_pose.mp4
        {clip_name}_keyframes.json
    averaged/
      {dance_name}_averaged.json
      {dance_name}_confidence.json

## Style rules
- Python 3.10+, type hints on all function signatures
- f-strings only, no .format() or % formatting
- Print prefixes: [POSE] in extract_pose.py, [BATCH] in process_dance.py, [AVG] in average_dance.py
- No print spam in frame loops — use tqdm progress bars
- All constants loaded from pipeline_config.yaml, never hardcoded
- Comments in plain English, concise
- No em dashes in comments or docstrings

## What is NOT built yet (do not generate code for these)
- Phase 4: Isaac Sim playback
- Phase 5: config-driven adjustment loop
- Phase 6: real robot deployment

## Pose estimator priority
1. ViTPose via mmpose (preferred)
2. MediaPipe Holistic (fallback)
Active estimator is recorded in pipeline_config.yaml under `pose_estimator`.